  <title id="bdl19regressionhmc-title">Deep ensemble and factorized VI compared with an HMC reference on one-dimensional regression</title>
  <desc id="bdl19regressionhmc-desc">Three regression panels with inputs from minus 10 to 10 show the same data in three clusters separated by two gaps, a thick predictive mean and shaded one and two standard deviation bands. (a) The HMC reference has narrow bands on the data and wider bands in the gaps and at the edges. (b) The deep ensemble looks very similar; the strip above it shows a small input-wise Wasserstein discrepancy. (c) Factorized VI keeps a narrow band everywhere, including between the data clusters; its strip shows a larger discrepancy, highest in the gaps. (d) Average Wasserstein discrepancy against the number of samples from 1 to 50: the deep-ensemble curve falls from about 0.16 to about 0.09, while the SVI curve stays near 0.14 to 0.15.</desc>
